 ### Priority
 
@@ -118,17 +118,30 @@ ### Ordering and Fairness
 
 The **next candidate queue** is **deterministic**: same state input → same next ticket, no random draw.
 
+**Implementation (`App\Actions\CallNextTicket`):** a ticket is **normal** when `priority = 0` and **priority** when `priority > 0`. Candidates are `waiting` tickets of the given queue only; called tickets are never called again.
+
+- **Full ordering:** `priority` desc, then `issued_at` asc, then `id` asc.
+- **Fairness (`any` mode only):** look at the last 3 tickets called in the queue (`called_at` desc, then `id` desc). If there are 3, all are priority, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, the call is restricted to the oldest waiting normal ticket. Otherwise full ordering applies. A normal call resets the streak. Calls made in `priority_only` / `normal_only` mode count in this history.
+- **`priority_only`:** only priority candidates, full ordering, fairness ignored.
+- **`normal_only`:** only normal candidates, oldest first, fairness ignored.
+- **Inactive queue:** `InactiveQueueException`; the `is_active` flag is read from the database under the queue-row lock, never from the caller's instance.
+- **No eligible ticket** (empty queue, only normals in `priority_only`, only priority in `normal_only`): `NoWaitingTicketsException`.
+- Both exceptions leave the database unchanged.
+- **Exactly-once:** the queue row is locked for the whole call. The chosen ticket is then locked and re-checked as still `waiting`, and skipped if it was called concurrently through `Ticket::call()` (which takes no queue lock).
+- **Result:** the winner gets `status=called`, `called_at=now()` and `called_by_user_id`; no other field changes. The action returns the updated ticket.
+- **Authorization** is not part of the action. The caller (HTTP/Livewire layer, future work) must authorize before calling it.
+
 ### Call Panel (attendant)
 
-Three explicit actions, all deterministic:
+Three explicit actions, all deterministic. Each maps to a `CallMode` passed to `CallNextTicket`:
 
-| Button | Behavior |
-| ----- | ------------- |
-| **Next (most important)** | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
-| **Priority** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
-| **Normal** | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among normal candidates. |
+| Button | `CallMode` | Behavior |
+| ----- | ----- | ------------- |
+| **Next (most important)** | `any` | Calls the next ticket according to full ordering (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness rule). |
+| **Priority** | `priority_only` | Calls the next eligible ticket **only** among priority candidates (includes 80+ per configuration). |
